from pathlib import Path
import json,hashlib
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
rows=[
('An Exile takes the Oathkeeper title during their Act phase. When can they first win as Usurper, and what happens if someone takes the title away meanwhile?', 'At their next Wake they check victory before flipping Oathkeeper to Usurper, so cannot yet win as Usurper; if still Usurper at the following Wake they win. Losing the title prevents this; a new holder receives it Oathkeeper-side. At end of round eight an existing Usurper can win under the ordered endgame rules.', 'Law 2.11, 3.1, 3.4, 4.1.2–3'),
('List all four Oaths, their matching Visions, and the extra universal requirement for a Visionary win. Do ties for most count for a Vision?', 'Supremacy/Conquest: most sites; People/Rebellion: People’s Favor; Protection/Sanctuary: most relics and banners combined; Devotion/Faith: Darkest Secret. Exile must have the Vision revealed, fulfill it at Wake (or the round-eight check), and at least three Visions must have been drawn from the world deck. Most means strictly more than every other player, not a tie.', 'Law 2.11,3.2,3.4; Errata 3.2'),
('When are end dice rolled, what results end the game, and can an Exile Oathkeeper permit such a roll?', 'Only at end of rounds five/six/seven with Chancellor or Citizen Oathkeeper: 6 / 5–6 / 3–6 respectively. Exile Oathkeeper prevents the roll. Eighth round ends automatically.', 'Law 3.3,3.4'),
('At round eight, what is the complete victory priority including simultaneous Visions and Citizens?', 'Empire if Chancellor/Citizen Oathkeeper, then Exile Usurper, then qualifying Exile Visionary (Conquest > Rebellion > Sanctuary > Faith), then Empire fallback. Each Empire win is Chancellor unless a Citizen fulfills the Successor goal, who wins alone instead.', 'Law 3.3.1,3.4; Playbook p26'),
('Give the Successor goal for each Oath. May a Citizen win by a revealed Vision or becoming Usurper?', 'Supremacy: more relics+banners than Chancellor and every other Citizen; People: Darkest Secret; Protection: People’s Favor; Devotion: Grand Scepter. Citizens do not win by Usurper or Vision, only replace a Chancellor win via succession.', 'Law 3.3.1,3.1–2'),
('Resolve the People’s Favor at Wake, including the Mob side, its last favor, and when the Mob threshold is checked.', 'First choose to put one board favor on it or move one from it to least-full bank (choose ties); it cannot lose its last favor, so at one must add if able, otherwise nothing. Repeat that step once if already Mob. After these steps flip to Mob if six or more favor. Then check Exile wins, flip Oathkeeper, and resolve optional opportunity-site income.', 'Law 4.1'),
('What happens in Rest, in order, and how do Citizen Supply and saved Supply work?', 'Return favor from denizens/edifices to matching banks; secrets from denizens/edifices/relics to acting board and flip own facedown secrets up; Exile/Chancellor refresh to personal-bank-warband space, Citizen to exact Chancellor marker space including leftmost; add remaining unspent Supply by moving left, capped at leftmost; optional Rest powers once each any order.', 'Law 4.3; Errata 4.3.3'),
('Explain Search sources/costs and how drawing a Vision differs between world deck and discard pile.', 'Choose only world deck or own-region discard, 2 Supply for discard, world cost 2 at zero Visions, 3 at one/two, 4 at three–five, modified by powers (Darkest Secret makes world draw 2). Draw up to three available; from world one at a time, announce a Vision, stop immediately and increment track; discard Vision does neither. Discard all but one before playing or discarding that one.', 'Law 5.1; Playbook p12,32; map Visions Drawn track'),
('Where do discarded cards and resources on them go, including a card at a remote site?', 'Facedown atop next-region pile: Cradle→Provinces→Hinterland→Cradle, acting player chooses order. Base on pawn region for drawn/adviser cards; if discarding a card in a different region, use that card’s region. Favor immediately goes to matching bank; secrets to acting board facedown.', 'Law Glossary Discard'),
('How do adviser limits, facedown restrictions, revealing later, and replacing a true Vision work?', 'Three advisers including facedown; facedown has no suit/banner/power, any card can be held thus. Before playing over limit discard an adviser, respecting locks and any new changed limit. Minor action may play facedown adviser faceup as searched (site/advisers/revealed Vision as legal) or discard it. True faceup Vision only Exile revealed slot, not adviser, replaces/discards existing Vision. Cannot simply discard faceup adviser at will.', 'Law 5.1.4,6.1,7.2,7.6.4; Errata 7.6.4'),
('What are Muster and both Trade costs, eligible cards, gains, destinations, and limitations when no advisers match?', 'Only empty denizen/intact edifice at pawn site, no favor/secrets; not relic/ruin. Muster 1 Supply+one favor on card → two personal-bank warbands to board, purple for Citizen. Trade 1 Supply; one secret on card → one favor+one per matching faceup adviser from matching bank; or two favor on card → one shared-bank secret per matching faceup adviser (zero if none). Finite source shortfall gives as much as possible.', 'Law 5.2–3,9.3'),
('How do you Recover a relic versus either banner, and what happens to the old banner resources?', '1 Supply; facedown relic at pawn site only at printed site cost, then take faceup personal bank. Either banner from anywhere, even yourself: pay more favor/secrets than old amount, stack new payment. People’s Favor flips off Mob and old favor distributes singly along banks away from deck from any starting suit wrapping. Darkest Secret: take one old secret, previous holder gets rest (self gets all; bank remainder stays bank).', 'Law 5.4; banner placards'),
('When is another player’s Darkest Secret safe or recoverable? Include no advisers, no cards, and a ruin-only site.', 'Recoverable if at least one suited card at holder’s pawn site matches none of their faceup advisers; no faceup advisers does not protect it if suited card exists. Empty/ruin-only site protects it; ignore suits absent on ruins/facedown advisers. Can recover from self or shared bank freely, still paying cost.', 'Law 5.4.1 corrected by Errata 5.4; banner'),
('Explain legal Campaign defender and target selection, including remote sites and a same-site relic target.', '2 Supply; defender another player ruling pawn site or whose pawn there, or bandits if no player rules it. At least one target at pawn site; if defender rules it must target it. May target any defender sites anywhere; relics/banners or pawn+favor only if their pawn is at attacker site. Relic target of co-located defender satisfies local target requirement. Pawn+favor adds two defense dice; sites one each; relic printed shields; banners resource count.', 'Law 5.5.1–2; Errata 5.5.2'),
('How are Campaign attack/defense calculated, and how do skulls, hollow swords, ties and sacrifices work?', 'Attacker chooses up to board-force warbands worth of attack dice. Defense shields multiplied by each double (x2,x4,...), plus warbands at targeted sites and defender board if pawn at attacker or targeted site; bandits one per targeted site. Attack skulls kill own force immediately; paired hollow swords count one, lone hollow zero. Attack must strictly exceed defense; may sacrifice force warbands +1 each, exactly enough to win, no excess; if unable/decline defender wins.', 'Law 5.5.2,5.5.4–6,9.5'),
('After an attacker wins, resolve defeat and all targets, including choosing zero garrisons, banner seizure, and banishment.', 'Defeated force kills half rounded down; remaining returns to board; defeated effects. Attacker may move any number including zero from force onto targeted sites, takes all targeted relics/banners; seized banners burn two resources to min one, People’s Favor becomes Mob. If pawn+favor targeted may banish to legal chosen site for no Supply and may burn half favor rounded down. Shrouded Wood can override destination. Victory effects then end-discard plans.', 'Law 5.5.6–8,2.5.3'),
('What changes in a Campaign involving Imperial defenders or a Citizen attacking another Imperial player?', 'Citizen attacker against Chancellor/Citizen is non-Imperial for that Campaign; Citizen targeted by Chancellor likewise. Imperial defender gets Chancellor automatically as Ally; non-attacker Citizens may join with permission if pawn at targeted site or attacker site. Activate defender/allies modifiers, share side powers and battle plans, one use per plan paid by user, never another’s advisers; qualifying allied board warbands defend. Chancellor chooses losses; survivors at sites go Chancellor board, Citizens keep own board survivors. Declared defender decides contested timing/order. Oathkeeper defense bonus shared even non-Supremacy.', 'Law 5.5,2.11; Errata 5.5'),
('State all base Travel costs and what happens when a facedown destination is revealed. How do fixed costs, increases and free Travel interact?', 'Cradle→Cradle 1, Provinces 2, Hinterland 4; Provinces→any other site 2; Hinterland→Hinterland 3, Provinces 2, Cradle 4. Move pawn, reveal site and add printed favor/secrets from shared bank and facedown relics from relic deck. Apply fixed-number Travel cost first then other modifiers; spend-no-Supply overrides all increases. Pawn movement does not move site warbands.', 'Law 5.6,7.6.2; Errata 5.6'),
('How can Citizenship be offered and accepted during play, and what may or must be exchanged?', 'Grand Scepter holder (not taken this turn) offers any Exile including self exactly one Reliquary relic plus optional binding exchange favor,secrets,banners,non-Reliquary relics. Accepted: flip Citizen, replace all board/map warbands purple as available with recipient choosing shortfall removals/replacements, discard revealed Vision, Usurper→Oathkeeper, end Act if own turn, refresh full. Exchange agreed items; Chancellor gains uncovered mandatory modifier. All Imperials rule purple sites. Reliquary relics inaccessible to Campaign/Recover, powers unusable, do not count goals.', 'Law 2.3,6.6; Grand Scepter'),
('Describe the Chronicle’s new Oath choice, Citizenship turnover, and world-deck rebuilding, including why the top stack is not 14 cards.', 'Vision-only winner uses matching Oath; other/multiple-method win chooses any different Oath. Exile winner flips all Citizens even boxed to Exile then may offer other Exiles except newly flipped; accepted map garrisons replaced one each by winner warband (ignore normal offer). Rebuild remaining denizens: ten+two random Visions=12 top, fifteen+three Visions=18 middle, remaining denizens bottom. Chronicle aid 12 denizens+2 is erroneous.', 'Law 8.1–2,8.8; Errata 8.2 and Chronicle Aid')]
q={'game':'Oath: Chronicles of Empire and Exile','scope':'2021 base first printing; Law October 20 2020 + full Playbook; official base errata November 15 2022; multiplayer, Chronicle and later setup; no bots or expansions','benchmark_version':'seed-v1','questions':[]}
k={'benchmark_version':'seed-v1','grading_standard':{'correct':'All requested parts correct with no contradiction or unresolved caveat and supported by summary.','partial':'Missing or unresolved requested part, no material contradiction.','incorrect':'Any material contradiction.'},'selection':'Source-first; canonical summary did not exist when seed designed.','answers':[]}
for n,(question,answer,refs) in enumerate(rows,1):
 id=f'Q{n:03}';q['questions'].append({'id':id,'question':question});k['answers'].append({'id':id,'expected_answer':answer,'material_facts':answer.split('; '),'source_references':refs})
d=P/'seed-v1';d.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
for name,data in [('questions.json',q),('answer-key.json',k)]: (d/name).write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
(d/'question-bank.md').write_text('# Oath seed bank v1\n\n'+'\n\n'.join(f"## {a['id']}\n\n{b['question']}\n\n**Answer:** {a['expected_answer']}\n\n**Source:** {a['source_references']}" for a,b in zip(k['answers'],q['questions']))+'\n')
(d/'input-manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps({f:hashlib.sha256((d/f).read_bytes()).hexdigest() for f in ['questions.json','answer-key.json']},indent=2)+'\n')
